    3. **Descriptive Alts**: The 'alternative' field must explain HOW the substitution changes the dish (e.g., "Yogurt instead of Cream: Lighter and tangier, add a pinch of sugar to balance").
    4. **Local Context**: Heavily favor Bangladeshi flavor profiles and staples (Rice, Dal, Mustard Oil, Green Chilies, Turmeric).

    Instructional Style:
    - Beginner-friendly, visual cues (e.g., "until the oil separates from the masala"), and precise heat settings.
    - Provide structured JSON output.
  `;

  const response = await ai.models.generateContent({
    model,
    contents: `The user has these items in stock: ${pantryItems.join(", ")}. Suggest a creative recipe. If common staples are missing, be very clever with substitutions.`,
    config: {
      systemInstruction,
      responseMimeType: "application/json",
      responseSchema: {
        type: Type.OBJECT,
        properties: {
          title: { type: Type.STRING },
          description: { type: Type.STRING },
          prepTime: { type: Type.STRING },
          servings: { type: Type.NUMBER },
          ingredients: { type: Type.ARRAY, items: { type: Type.STRING } },
          instructions: { type: Type.ARRAY, items: { type: Type.STRING } },
          bangladeshiContext: { type: Type.STRING },
          missingIngredientsDetails: {
            type: Type.ARRAY,
            items: {
              type: Type.OBJECT,
              properties: {
                name: { 
                  type: Type.STRING, 
                  description: "The name of the missing ingredient." 
                },
                alternative: { 
                  type: Type.STRING, 
                  description: "A context-aware, descriptive substitution explanation including flavor profile adjustments." 
                }
              },
              required: ["name", "alternative"]
            }
          }
        },
        required: ["title", "description", "prepTime", "ingredients", "instructions", "missingIngredientsDetails"]
      }
    }
  });

  return JSON.parse(response.text || "{}");
};

